WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.468
This is an exciting

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.937
moment for AI here in Canada.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.539
We are facing a historic opportunity

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.375
and responsibility

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.110
to harness the potential of AI

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.678
to drive economic growth

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.713
and improve social outcomes.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.583
Canada is AI’s birthplace,

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.450
and I'm proud to say

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.852
that much of the seminal work

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.920
happened and continues to happen

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.689
right here in Toronto.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.890
Among Canada's

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.892
early investments was the founding

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.694
of the Vector Institute,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.695
led by our Chief

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.064
Scientific Advisor Geoffrey Hinton.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.998
With the support

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.333
of the Government of Canada,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.601
the Government of Ontario,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.269
and industry partners,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:39.706
Vector helped make Ontario a hub of AI

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.307
excellence that has spilled out

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.609
across Canada,

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.711
leading to the tremendous growth

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.979
of our AI industry.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.815
Last year alone, more than $8.6B

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.749
in venture capital

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.085
funding was invested in Canadian

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:52.986
AI companies.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:56.156
That's 30% of all Canadian VC activity.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.191
That is a stunning number

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.693
for an industry that didn't even exist

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.328
less than a decade ago.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.864
Generative AI is already transforming

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.699
the way we work and play.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.902
Canada is home to many generative AI

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.170
focused companies.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.071
At Vector,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.372
we’re highly focused

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.074
on helping Canadian industry

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.209
adopt and commercialize AI.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.877
We work with our industry partners

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.412
to give their teams unique

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.114
access to expert

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.583
researchers, exceptional training,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.118
and a sandbox environment

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.587
that allows them to experiment with new

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.855
AI technologies.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.824
They know that in partnering with Vector,

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.026
they gain unparalleled access

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.894
to an AI talent pool

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.229
that really sets the bar

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.897
for the rest of the world.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.699
AI holds tremendous

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.934
promise to improve our daily

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.969
lives, our society,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.938
and our economic prospects

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.740
as long as we do it responsibly.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.678
This moment in AI in Canada really

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.545
excites me.

